# Coverage ratchet baseline (CI-002) — the measured value, not a target.
#
# Read by scripts/check-coverage.sh, which fails the run if coverage falls more
# than 2 points below this number. Raising it is a deliberate, reviewable act:
# add the tests that close the gap, then move the number in the same commit.
#
# Measured 2026-09-25 on `feat/ingest-ledger-idempotent-writes` (SUB-002, the per-class run):
#   pytest --cov=garsync -m "not e2e"   301 passed, 1034 statements, 135 missed
#   TOTAL 87% (86.94)
#
# Raised from 85.88 by the run's own tests (AC1/AC4/AC5) and by two guards that close branches the
# suite had never reached: `Window.days()` refusing to enumerate a minute-resolved class, and
# `activity_to_row` reading the UTC instant out of the payload instead of a zone. `repository.py`,
# `connection.py`, `payload.py` remain at 100%; `window.py` and `pipeline.py` are at 99%, each missing
# one line that only a real clock reaches (`_utc_now`).
#
# Measured 2026-09-25 on `feat/ingest-ledger-idempotent-writes` (SUB-002, ledger counts — block 4):
#   pytest --cov=garsync -m "not e2e"   277 passed, 1020 statements, 144 missed
#   TOTAL 86% (85.88)
#
# Raised from 85.17, and the gap it closes was measured two commits ago: the idempotency suite (block
# 3) carried the tree to 85.67 without moving this file, because the tick that says "raise the ratchet
# only if the new tests lift it" lives in block 7 and nobody had read it back yet. A ratchet that lags
# the tests it is supposed to defend lets a later commit delete coverage and still pass, so it is set
# to what the tree measures now, in the commit that adds the tests keeping it there — `TestLedgerCounts`
# and `0003_ledger_counts`, whose two columns and NULL-on-purpose default are the new statements. The
# rest of the diff is the pipeline extraction, which measured the same before and after.
#
# Measured 2026-09-25 on `feat/ingest-ledger-idempotent-writes` (SUB-002, first cycle — the window
# rule):
#   pytest --cov=garsync -m "not e2e"   236 passed, 971 statements, 144 missed
#   TOTAL 85% (85.17)
#
# Raised from 84.07 by the tests that arrived with `src/garsync/ingest/window.py` — 64 of the 67 new
# statements, covered 100% by the fifteen table-driven cases that pin the coverage watermark (settle,
# granularity, the 14-day floor, gap chunking, the DST fold, the ≈71-call arithmetic).
#
# Measured 2026-09-25 on `feat/alembic-schema-migration` (SUB-001):
#   pytest --cov=garsync -m "not e2e"   219 passed, 904 statements, 144 missed
#   TOTAL 84% (84.07)
#
# Raised from 83.03 in the SUB-001 commit, which added 144 statements (two Alembic revisions, the
# connection bridge, the backup, the UTC helpers) and the tests that cover them — including the
# migration rehearsal against a copy of the real database. The number moved because the tests
# arrived with the code, which is the only way this file is allowed to move.
#
# What still drags it down, so the next reader knows where the headroom is:
#   src/garsync/client.py      18%   (network client, exercised through mocks only)
#   src/garsync/exporter.py     0%   (declared, not yet wired to a route or the CLI)
